            "rawRagKnowledge": {
              "query": "Messages disappear when clicking on notifications in Twake Chat, leaving the channel empty.",
              "content": "```json\n{\n  \"candidates\": [\n    {\n      \"rawKnowledge\": \"This GitHub issue details a bug in the Tmail Flutter app where deleted emails persist on the mobile app until a manual refresh, while the web app behaves correctly; the issue was resolved by updating the sync mechanism to handle deleted messages via `/changes` and push notifications.\\n\\n## Metadata\\nRepository: linagora/tmail-flutter\\nIssue number: 2453\\nState: closed\\nAuthor: guimard\\nCreated at: 2024-01-14T12:22:08Z\\nUpdated at: 2025-05-07T20:08:48Z\\nClosed at: 2024-04-03T07:51:26Z\\nLabels: bug\\nAssignees:\\nURL: https://github.com/linagora/tmail-flutter/issues/2453\\n\\n## Issue body\\n\\n### Description\\n\\nWhen deleting mails with another mail client, Tmail app still shoes this deleted messages\\n\\n### Expected result\\n\\nSynchronization should detect that mail were modified/deleted. The app should never show a deleted email when it is online and able to detect this deletion\\n\\n### Current behavior\\n\\nMessage deleted are still present in mobile app (not web app)\\n\\n### Context\\n\\nThunderbird on desktop, Tmail on Android\\n\\n## Comments\\n\\n### Comment by chibenwa at 2024-01-15T07:30:48Z\\n\\nThanks for the remark Xavier.\\n\\nOn a technical standpoint `Email/changes` returns `destroyed` mail ids. Those can be dropped straight away from the cache. We can detect the need to call `/changes` by relying on push notifications.\\n\\n### Comment by QuangHoang1210 at 2024-01-15T08:45:27Z\\n\\nHi @guimard and @chibenwa cc @hoangdat\\n\\nI have reproduce this case.\\n\\nStep:\\n1, I removed one email from Samsung email\\n2, I have check again that email in Twake Mail (Samsung app, IOS app)\\n\\nActual: The email is removed\\n--> So it catch our expectation\\n\\n**Noted:**\\n- But we should do one refresh action (scroll to reload, refresh) then the email will be disappeared\\n- I have tried to removed the 1st email, 23th email, 52th emails -> Same\\n\\n**Video**\\n\\nhttps://github.com/linagora/tmail-flutter/assets/124866146/19690622-499c-4985-a3e7-f745bb19e20c\",\n      \"whyPotentiallyRelevant\": \"This issue involves synchronization problems in the Twake Mail app, where deleted messages persist until a manual refresh. Although it pertains to email messages rather than chat messages, the underlying synchronization mechanism might be relevant to the chat notification issue.\",\n      \"sourceHint\": \"github_linagora_tmail_flutter_issue_2453.md\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```",
              "candidates": [
                {
                  "rawKnowledgeId": "raw_knowledge_1",
                  "rawKnowledge": "This GitHub issue details a bug in the Tmail Flutter app where deleted emails persist on the mobile app until a manual refresh, while the web app behaves correctly; the issue was resolved by updating the sync mechanism to handle deleted messages via `/changes` and push notifications.\n\n## Metadata\nRepository: linagora/tmail-flutter\nIssue number: 2453\nState: closed\nAuthor: guimard\nCreated at: 2024-01-14T12:22:08Z\nUpdated at: 2025-05-07T20:08:48Z\nClosed at: 2024-04-03T07:51:26Z\nLabels: bug\nAssignees:\nURL: https://github.com/linagora/tmail-flutter/issues/2453\n\n## Issue body\n\n### Description\n\nWhen deleting mails with another mail client, Tmail app still shoes this deleted messages\n\n### Expected result\n\nSynchronization should detect that mail were modified/deleted. The app should never show a deleted email when it is online and able to detect this deletion\n\n### Current behavior\n\nMessage deleted are still present in mobile app (not web app)\n\n### Context\n\nThunderbird on desktop, Tmail on Android\n\n## Comments\n\n### Comment by chibenwa at 2024-01-15T07:30:48Z\n\nThanks for the remark Xavier.\n\nOn a technical standpoint `Email/changes` returns `destroyed` mail ids. Those can be dropped straight away from the cache. We can detect the need to call `/changes` by relying on push notifications.\n\n### Comment by QuangHoang1210 at 2024-01-15T08:45:27Z\n\nHi @guimard and @chibenwa cc @hoangdat\n\nI have reproduce this case.\n\nStep:\n1, I removed one email from Samsung email\n2, I have check again that email in Twake Mail (Samsung app, IOS app)\n\nActual: The email is removed\n--> So it catch our expectation\n\n**Noted:**\n- But we should do one refresh action (scroll to reload, refresh) then the email will be disappeared\n- I have tried to removed the 1st email, 23th email, 52th emails -> Same\n\n**Video**\n\nhttps://github.com/linagora/tmail-flutter/assets/124866146/19690622-499c-4985-a3e7-f745bb19e20c",
                  "whyPotentiallyRelevant": "This issue involves synchronization problems in the Twake Mail app, where deleted messages persist until a manual refresh. Although it pertains to email messages rather than chat messages, the underlying synchronization mechanism might be relevant to the chat notification issue.",
                  "sourceHint": "github_linagora_tmail_flutter_issue_2453.md"
                }
              ],
